WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.979
One of the things that we've really been trying
to figure out is what is the real rate of

00:00:05.979 --> 00:00:10.890
Corona virus infection, because the official
numbers only tell us the number of people

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:14.780
that have actually had a test and tested positive
for the disease.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:19.970
But of course, there's a whole bunch of people
who have or have had Corona virus without

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:23.740
being tested, many of whom have already recovered.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:29.699
And one of the ways you can test for the real
rate is to do an antibody test, the antibodies

00:00:29.699 --> 00:00:34.730
produced by the body in the process of or
after finishing the process of fighting the

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:35.730
virus.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:39.190
But there have been antibody tests that have
not been accurate.

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:41.899
So that has not been particularly useful.

00:00:41.899 --> 00:00:47.100
There have also been studies that have tested
sewage and depending on which test you look

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.100
at.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:53.280
We've heard that the real infection rate could
be as small as two times the official rate

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:56.539
or as large as 250 times the official rate.

00:00:56.539 --> 00:01:03.890
Now, I've said before only two times the official
rate sounds low to me, 250 times the official

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:06.000
rate sounds too high to me.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.260
If it were 250 times the official rate, we'd
be talking about roughly 200 million Americans

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:13.640
with Corona virus.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:18.520
And that does not seem to pass the sniff test,
although if it were true, we would potentially

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:20.240
be close to herd immunity.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.159
But it doesn't pass the sniff test.

00:01:22.159 --> 00:01:29.329
So in looking at different data, my thought
has been the real number of infections is

00:01:29.329 --> 00:01:36.220
somewhere between four and 30 times the official
number, which is still a very big range.

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:40.970
We have a new study from Los Angeles County
that is looking at exactly this question.

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:43.479
What is the real rate of infection?

00:01:43.479 --> 00:01:48.750
They went and they gave antibody tests to
a random sample of eight hundred and sixty

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:49.750
three adults.

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:54.119
And they found that somewhere between two
hundred and twenty thousand four hundred and

00:01:54.119 --> 00:01:59.600
forty thousand people in Los Angeles County
have already been infected.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:05.869
Now, when you compare those numbers to the
official case, number of just under 14000

00:02:05.869 --> 00:02:13.170
at the time that the study was done, this
study implies that the real infection number

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:19.480
is somewhere between 15 and 30 times the official
case number.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:24.470
Now, if we apply that to the entire United
States, it would suggest between 12 and 24

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:29.800
million people have or have had Corona virus
so far or really have had, because you don't

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:32.129
have antibodies when you're actively infected.

00:02:32.129 --> 00:02:35.050
Now, as always, there's a bunch of caveats
here.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:38.950
One is no one's study is likely to be the
one.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:42.220
Infection rates are realistically different
and different different parts of the country.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:48.269
And importantly, even if this is correct,
we would be nowhere near herd immunity at

00:02:48.269 --> 00:02:49.909
this point in time.

00:02:49.909 --> 00:02:56.379
The good news, if the real rate of infection
is 15 to 30 times the official rate is it

00:02:56.379 --> 00:03:02.659
implies a far lower fatality rate than we
think because a much smaller portion of people

00:03:02.659 --> 00:03:03.659
are dying.

00:03:03.659 --> 00:03:08.220
If you have a thousand deaths out of ten thousand
infections, that's much more serious than

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:11.239
if you have a thousand deaths out of 100000
infections.

00:03:11.239 --> 00:03:17.959
Now, the bad news of the real rate being 15
to 30 times the official rate is that it means

00:03:17.959 --> 00:03:21.450
the virus spreads way more easily than we
thought.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:27.689
And we are nowhere near having a testing system
that can actually identify a large portion

00:03:27.689 --> 00:03:28.720
of the cases.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:33.989
If you can identify cases, you can't contact
trace, you can't tell people who might have

00:03:33.989 --> 00:03:36.930
been exposed that they need to quarantine.

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:39.750
But as always, any one study can be way off.

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:45.069
We've learned that some antibody tests are
just very an accurate fundamentally.

00:03:45.069 --> 00:03:51.100
Technically speaking, I believe some of those
tests may have been used in this study.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:56.959
The other thing to keep in mind is the more
you test, the closer you are to the real infection

00:03:56.959 --> 00:03:57.959
rate.

00:03:57.959 --> 00:03:59.640
So I want to be really clear about this.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:04.980
We can't just take the nationwide number and
multiply it by 15 to 30 based on the L.A.

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:05.980
County results.

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:06.980
Why not?

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.489
I'll give you an example.

00:04:08.489 --> 00:04:12.720
New York is testing way more than California.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:18.850
New York has tested 33000 people for every
million in the population, whereas California

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:24.090
has only tested 7000 people for every million
in the population.

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:28.440
Since California has not been testing as much
as New York.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:36.380
We would imagine that the real infection rate
in California is many times higher than the

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:41.080
real infection rate in New York because New
York has tested more people.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.560
That's what we know right now.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:44.810
Someday we'll have a good antibody test.

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:46.540
We can rely on.

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:51.440
We'll figure out what the real penetrance
of the disease has been across the country.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:52.880
We're not there yet.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:05:07.060
And the reality that we have right now is
we are certainly undercounting cases.

00:05:07.060 --> 00:06:11.280
We 
just don't.

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:35.090
Know exactly by how much

